{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1rfM2JJFA25GUzhXMJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Recommendation: build it, but build it as an experiment, and spend a day or two on one reach check first.**\n\n**What the evidence supports.** The email trial is solid. Patients were randomly assigned, about 400 per arm, and late collection fell 13 points (31% → 18%). The 95% confidence interval is roughly ±6 points, so the effect is real. The control group's 31% matches the pharmacy-wide rate, so the email opt-in patients don't look unusual.\n\n**What it doesn't tell you.**\n- **Reach:** Push only helps patients who have the app installed with notifications turned on. If few late collectors have the app, push can't move the 31% much, however well it works per person. Pulling that number from your data is a day's work, and it determines whether this is worth building.\n- **Channel:** Push may work better or worse than email. It's more immediate but easier to swipe away. You can't assume the 13 points carry over.\n- **Overlap:** Many app users may already get the email. What matters is the extra effect of push on top of email, which is probably smaller.\n\n**Two cheaper steps to take alongside:**\n1. Roll out the email reminder to everyone who has opted in, if you haven't already. It's proven and costs almost nothing.\n2. Use the three weeks to build push with a randomised holdout: push vs no push, split by whether the patient already gets the email. Measure late collection, not opens. This answers the questions above with your own data, and more research beforehand wouldn't give you that.\n\n**One build requirement:** Lock-screen notifications shouldn't show medication names. That's a privacy issue, so get the wording approved early."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3193,"cache_read_input_tokens":5027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3193},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0b5a981-bc49-48b5-af23-8ce53aa80353","uuid":"4d432e6f-958a-4795-aa0e-2f9f58d03e67","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:17:43.652Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1rf69XQNt75tLeaf5a"}
